                <head>Appendix E to HD–66</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Telegram From the British Delegation
                        to General Haking</hi>]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Cypher telegram to General Malcolm, Berlin, from Astoria, D.
                    17:30, 25 September 1919.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 60</p>
                <p>M. Paderewski suggests immediate despatch of a considerable number of allied
                    officers to Upper Silesia to safeguard the interests of inhabitants and ensure
                    normal output of coal.</p>
                <p>Telegraph your views as to practicability and desirability of above proposal, and
                    state number of allied officers already in Upper Silesia. This suggestion is
                    entirely distinct from question of dispatching plebiscite Commissioners who
                    could not in any case now proceed prior to ratification.</p>
            </div>
